 - Writes require the `contributor` or `manager` role in the project. Users who can read but not write get 403.
 - Contributors may only modify tasks assigned to themselves, and may not reassign tasks. Managers may modify any task.
 - Only managers may delete tasks.
+- Moving a task (`/move`) needs a manager of the source project (not archived), and a contributor or manager of the destination project (not archived; 403 if the actor can only read it, 409 if archived). A destination that is missing, in another organization, or not readable → 404. The move keeps the task's ID, title, status and assignee; if the assignee is not a contributor or manager of the destination, the move is rejected with 400. Moving a task to the project it is already in → 400.
 - Archived projects reject all writes with 409 (reads still work).
 - A task ID that does not belong to the project in the path → 404.
 
